{"openapi":"3.1.0","info":{"title":"MemberArea API","version":"1.0.0","description":"The MemberArea API exposes your MemberArea: members, courses, hubs, events,\nproducts, orders and the community, as a clean REST interface. All endpoints\nare scoped to the MemberArea that owns the API key.\n\n**Base URL:** `https://api.memberarea.io/v1`\n\n**Authentication:** Two credentials open the same API.\n\n- **API key**, the MemberArea's own credential, created by its owner under\n  Settings \u2192 API keys. Send it as `X-Api-Key: mak_\u2026` (preferred) or\n  `Authorization: Bearer mak_\u2026`. Right for your own scripts and for an\n  integration that serves one MemberArea.\n- **OAuth 2.0 access token**, for software that other MemberAreas connect.\n  An administrator approves your application on a consent screen and you\n  receive a token you send as `Authorization: Bearer mao_\u2026`. Nobody pastes\n  a key into your product, the grant covers only the scopes you asked for,\n  and it can be withdrawn at any time. The **OAuth** section below walks\n  the whole flow.\n\n**Scopes:** Every key carries an explicit list of scopes; each endpoint\nnames the one it needs. Where two are listed, either will do. The\n`wordpress:read` scope is meant for a key you hand to a website you connect:\nit opens only what such a site displays, and it narrows the answers, so\ndrafts, hidden entries and your own contact details stay out of reach.\nA few endpoints are not key-authenticated at all and say so.\n\n**Envelope:** Successful responses use `{ \"data\": ..., \"meta\": ... }`. Every\nerror carries `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"details\": ... } }`,\nincluding the ones raised before an endpoint runs (missing key, missing\nscope, rate limit) and every validation failure. Switch on `error.code`\nalone; you never need a second shape.\n\nErrors raised outside an endpoint additionally keep the framework's own\nkeys next to the envelope: `message`, plus `errors` with one array of\nmessages per rejected field on a validation failure. Those keys are kept\nfor clients written before the envelope was universal; `error.message`\nrepeats `message` and `error.details` repeats `errors`, so nothing is lost\nby reading the envelope only. Errors raised inside an endpoint carry the\nenvelope alone.\n\nMost codes are specific to the endpoint and named in its description. The\nones that can appear anywhere, derived from the status when nothing more\nprecise applies, are: `bad_request`, `unauthenticated`, `payment_required`,\n`forbidden`, `not_found`, `method_not_allowed`, `not_acceptable`,\n`conflict`, `gone`, `payload_too_large`, `unsupported_media_type`,\n`validation_failed`, `locked`, `rate_limited`, `not_implemented`,\n`service_unavailable` and `server_error`. An unrecognised code should be\ntreated by its HTTP status.\n\nOne documented exception: the automation webhook answers with a bare\n`{ \"error\": \"<code>\" }` string. It is a receiver, not an endpoint you call,\nand its shape is frozen so existing senders keep working. That endpoint is\nexcluded from the envelope entirely, including its framework-level errors.\n\n**Pagination:** List endpoints return up to 25 items by default. Pass\n`?per_page=50` (max 100) and `?page=N` to control pagination. `meta`\ncontains `page`, `per_page`, `total`, `last_page`.\n\n**IDs:** Resources are addressed by their `id` field, an opaque string.\nTreat it as a token: don't parse or construct it.\n\n**Rate limits:** Requests are metered per API key in staggered buckets:\n600 reads/min, 120 writes/min, and 30 automation triggers/min, plus daily\ncaps on top. Exceeding a bucket returns `429` with a `Retry-After` header\nand `X-RateLimit-*` headers describing the limit, the remaining budget and\nthe reset time.\n\n**Plan limits:** Write actions that would cross a plan boundary (for\nexample creating members beyond `limit_members`) are rejected with `402`\nand `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"plan_limit_reached\", ... } }`.\n"},"servers":[{"url":"https://api.memberarea.io/v1"}],"security":[{"ApiKeyHeader":[]},{"ApiKeyBearer":[]},{"OAuth2":[]}],"tags":[{"name":"Introspection","description":"Inspect the current API key."},{"name":"OAuth","description":"Connect other people's MemberAreas without ever handling their API key.\nYour software sends an administrator to a consent screen, receives an\nauthorization code, and exchanges it for an access token that is scoped\nto exactly one MemberArea.\n\nUse an API key when the credential belongs to the same party that runs\nthe code: your own scripts, an internal tool, a single customer you set\nup by hand. Use OAuth when your product is installed by many MemberAreas:\nthe administrator approves once, you never store their key, and they can\nwithdraw access without rotating anything else.\n\n**Registering your application.** Register it yourself in any MemberArea\nyou administer, under **Settings \u2192 OAuth Apps**. You give the app a name,\na short description and a website (all three appear on the consent\nscreen), one or more exact redirect URIs, and the scopes it may request.\nYou get a `client_id` (`mac_\u2026`) straight away, and a confidential client\nalso gets a `client_secret` (`mas_\u2026`) that is shown once and can be\nrotated later. Public clients (mobile, desktop, single-page apps) get no\nsecret and must use PKCE with S256.\n\nThe MemberArea you register in is only the home of the app record. The\napp itself is not tied to it: any MemberArea can connect, and every\ncustomer uses the same `client_id`. Request the fewest scopes you can,\nsince each one is listed on the consent screen the customer approves.\n\n**Endpoints.** The authorization server is `https://app.memberarea.io`,\nthe same host for every customer. It is described at\n`https://app.memberarea.io/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server`, so a\nclient library that reads OAuth discovery needs nothing else. The API\nitself stays on `https://api.memberarea.io/v1`: a token issued by the\nauthorization server works there without further ceremony.\n\n**Step 1: send the administrator to the consent screen.**\n\n```\nhttps://app.memberarea.io/oauth/authorize\n  ?response_type=code\n  &client_id=mac_\u2026\n  &redirect_uri=https://yourapp.example/callback\n  &scope=members:read%20members:write\n  &state=<random, verified on return>\n  &code_challenge=<BASE64URL(SHA256(verifier))>\n  &code_challenge_method=S256\n```\n\nThe screen signs the administrator in if needed, lists the requested\nscopes in plain language, and asks which of their MemberAreas to connect.\nScopes are space separated. Omitting `scope` asks for everything your\nclient is registered for, which is rarely what you want.\n\n**Step 2: take the code off your redirect URI.** We send the browser to\n`https://yourapp.example/callback?code=moc_\u2026&state=\u2026`. The redirect URI\nmust match a registered one character for character. A refusal arrives as\n`?error=access_denied&state=\u2026` instead, and an unknown client or\nunregistered redirect URI never redirects at all: it shows an error page,\nbecause sending anything to an unverified address would be the leak.\nCompare `state` with what you sent before you continue.\n\n**Step 3: exchange the code within 10 minutes.** One exchange per code.\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://app.memberarea.io/oauth/token \\\n  -d grant_type=authorization_code \\\n  -d client_id=mac_\u2026 \\\n  -d code=moc_\u2026 \\\n  -d redirect_uri=https://yourapp.example/callback \\\n  -d code_verifier=\u2026\n```\n\nA confidential client sends `client_secret` instead of `code_verifier`,\neither as a form field or as HTTP Basic credentials. The answer carries\n`access_token`, `token_type`, `expires_in`, `refresh_token` and the\ngranted `scope`.\n\n**Step 4: call the API.**\n\n```bash\ncurl https://api.memberarea.io/v1/me \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer mao_\u2026\"\n```\n\n`GET /me` names the MemberArea the token belongs to and is the natural\nfirst call after a connection: store that identity next to the token.\n\n**Step 5: refresh before the hour is out.** An access token lives 3600\nseconds, a refresh token 60 days. Every refresh rotates both:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://app.memberarea.io/oauth/token \\\n  -d grant_type=refresh_token \\\n  -d client_id=mac_\u2026 \\\n  -d refresh_token=mor_\u2026\n```\n\nPersist the new pair as one unit. The previous access token stops working\nthe moment the new one is issued, and replaying a spent refresh token\nreturns `invalid_grant`, so a client that keeps the old copy locks itself\nout on the next attempt.\n\n**What a token can reach.** One token, one MemberArea, chosen by the\nadministrator. Connecting a second one means running the flow again. The\ngranted scopes are the overlap between what you requested and what your\nclient is registered for, never more. A call outside them answers `403`\nwith `error.code` `missing_scope`, exactly as an under-scoped API key\nwould. Tokens are bearer credentials: keep them server side, out of logs\nand out of URLs.\n\n**Ending a connection.** Post the access or refresh token to\n`/oauth/revoke` when a customer disconnects your app. The administrator\ncan also revoke your grant from their MemberArea, and a grant dies on its\nown once the approving administrator loses admin rights there: the next\nrefresh then fails with `invalid_grant`. Treat any `invalid_grant` as\n\"the connection is gone\", drop the stored tokens and ask the customer to\nreconnect rather than retrying.\n\n**Plan gate.** The API is a Professional-plan feature. A token for a\nMemberArea on a smaller plan authenticates but every call answers `403`\nwith `error.code` `api_not_in_plan`. Surface that to the customer as an\nupgrade prompt, not as a broken connection.\n"},{"name":"Members","description":"People who joined your MemberArea."},{"name":"Tags","description":"Labels you attach to members."},{"name":"Custom Fields","description":"Per-MemberArea custom attributes on members."},{"name":"Global Fields","description":"Business-wide placeholder values, set once and reused everywhere."},{"name":"Groups","description":"Member groupings for access + organization."},{"name":"Courses","description":"E-learning courses and their modules."},{"name":"Lesson Content","description":"Author lessons, pages and elements, and import meeting recordings as lesson videos."},{"name":"Hubs","description":"Hub pages."},{"name":"Events","description":"Scheduled events."},{"name":"Products","description":"Catalog products (incl. bundles)."},{"name":"Orders","description":"Sales orders."},{"name":"Subscriptions","description":"Recurring subscription billing."},{"name":"Community","description":"Areas, forums, posts, comments, badges."},{"name":"Datasets","description":"Structured data collections and their rows."},{"name":"Hooks","description":"REST-hook subscriptions (Zapier / Make / custom)."},{"name":"Affiliates","description":"Affiliate program: register external conversions."},{"name":"Inbox","description":"Unified inbox: conversations, messages, tickets, labels, saved replies."},{"name":"Automations","description":"Automation workflows: inspect, trigger, and read runs."},{"name":"Contacts","description":"CRM contacts: people who are not yet members."},{"name":"Roles","description":"Member roles: presets and custom."},{"name":"Marketing","description":"Trust seals you can embed on external sites."},{"name":"WordPress","description":"Connected WordPress installations: registration, member sign-in, access checks."}],"paths":{"/oauth/authorize":{"servers":[{"url":"https://app.memberarea.io","description":"Authorization server. The same host for every MemberArea."}],"get":{"operationId":"oauthAuthorize","tags":["OAuth"],"summary":"Open the consent screen","security":[],"description":"Where the flow starts. Send the administrator's browser here, do not\ncall it from your backend. The screen handles sign-in, shows the\nrequested scopes and lets the administrator pick which MemberArea to\nconnect, then redirects back to your `redirect_uri` with a code.\n\nPKCE (`code_challenge` with `code_challenge_method=S256`) is mandatory\nfor public clients and recommended for everyone.\n","parameters":[{"in":"query","name":"response_type","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","enum":["code"]},"description":"Always `code`."},{"in":"query","name":"client_id","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","examples":["mac_9f2c\u2026"]},"description":"Your client id."},{"in":"query","name":"redirect_uri","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uri"},"description":"Must match a registered URI character for character."},{"in":"query","name":"scope","schema":{"type":"string","examples":["members:read members:write"]},"description":"Space-separated scopes. Omitted means everything your client may request."},{"in":"query","name":"state","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Returned unchanged. Compare it before you use the code."},{"in":"query","name":"code_challenge","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"BASE64URL(SHA256(code_verifier)), without padding."},{"in":"query","name":"code_challenge_method","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["S256"]},"description":"`S256`. Required whenever `code_challenge` is sent."}],"responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/OAuthUnexpectedError"},"200":{"description":"The consent screen as HTML.","content":{"text/html":{"schema":{"type":"string"}}}},"302":{"description":"The decision, as a redirect to your `redirect_uri`: `?code=moc_\u2026&state=\u2026` on approval, `?error=access_denied&state=\u2026` on refusal. `unsupported_response_type` and `invalid_scope` arrive the same way."},"400":{"description":"An HTML error page. The request never reaches your redirect URI because the client is unknown or inactive, or the redirect URI is not registered for it.","content":{"text/html":{"schema":{"type":"string"}}}}}}},"/oauth/token":{"servers":[{"url":"https://app.memberarea.io","description":"Authorization server. The same host for every MemberArea."}],"post":{"operationId":"oauthToken","tags":["OAuth"],"summary":"Exchange a code, or refresh a token","security":[],"description":"Server-to-server, `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`. Authorization\ncodes are single-use and expire after 10 minutes.\n\nA confidential client authenticates with `client_secret`, sent either\nas a form field or as HTTP Basic credentials (`client_id:client_secret`).\nA public client sends no secret and proves the exchange with\n`code_verifier`.\n\nEvery refresh rotates the access token and the refresh token. Store the\nnew pair together: the old access token stops working immediately and\nthe spent refresh token answers `invalid_grant`.\n","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/x-www-form-urlencoded":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["grant_type","client_id"],"properties":{"grant_type":{"type":"string","enum":["authorization_code","refresh_token"]},"client_id":{"type":"string","examples":["mac_9f2c\u2026"]},"client_secret":{"type":"string","description":"Confidential clients only."},"code":{"type":"string","description":"`authorization_code` grant. The `moc_\u2026` value from the redirect."},"redirect_uri":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"`authorization_code` grant. The same URI the code was issued for."},"code_verifier":{"type":"string","description":"`authorization_code` grant with PKCE. The plain verifier behind the challenge."},"refresh_token":{"type":"string","description":"`refresh_token` grant. The `mor_\u2026` value from the previous response."}}}}}},"responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/OAuthUnexpectedError"},"200":{"description":"A fresh token pair.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/OAuthTokenResponse"}}}},"400":{"description":"`invalid_grant` (code or refresh token unknown, expired, already used, issued to another client, or the approving administrator lost admin rights), `invalid_request` (a required field is missing), `unsupported_grant_type`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/OAuthError"}}}},"401":{"description":"`invalid_client`. Unknown client, inactive client, or a wrong secret.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/OAuthError"}}}}}}},"/oauth/revoke":{"servers":[{"url":"https://app.memberarea.io","description":"Authorization server. The same host for every MemberArea."}],"post":{"operationId":"oauthRevoke","tags":["OAuth"],"summary":"Revoke a token","security":[],"description":"Call this when a customer disconnects your application. Revoking either\nhalf of a pair ends the whole grant. Answers `200` whether or not the\ntoken existed, so a client cannot use it to probe for valid tokens.\n","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/x-www-form-urlencoded":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["token","client_id"],"properties":{"token":{"type":"string","description":"An access token (`mao_\u2026`) or a refresh token (`mor_\u2026`)."},"token_type_hint":{"type":"string","enum":["access_token","refresh_token"],"description":"Optional. Saves one lookup."},"client_id":{"type":"string"},"client_secret":{"type":"string","description":"Confidential clients only."}}}}}},"responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/OAuthUnexpectedError"},"200":{"description":"Revoked, or there was nothing to revoke."},"401":{"description":"`invalid_client`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/OAuthError"}}}}}}},"/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server":{"servers":[{"url":"https://app.memberarea.io","description":"Authorization server. The same host for every MemberArea."}],"get":{"operationId":"oauthDiscovery","tags":["OAuth"],"summary":"Authorization server metadata","security":[],"description":"RFC 8414 discovery. Point a standard OAuth client library at\n`https://app.memberarea.io` and it configures itself from here.\n\nThe document is host-relative: fetched from a MemberArea's own domain,\nit names that domain as the issuer. Pick one host and stay on it for\nthe whole flow.\n","responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/OAuthUnexpectedError"},"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"issuer":{"type":"string","format":"uri"},"authorization_endpoint":{"type":"string","format":"uri"},"token_endpoint":{"type":"string","format":"uri"},"registration_endpoint":{"type":"string","format":"uri"},"revocation_endpoint":{"type":"string","format":"uri"},"response_types_supported":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"grant_types_supported":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"code_challenge_methods_supported":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"token_endpoint_auth_methods_supported":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"scopes_supported":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}}}}}}}},"/me":{"get":{"operationId":"getMe","tags":["Introspection"],"summary":"Get current API key context","description":"Returns the key, the MemberArea it belongs to, and the linked user.","responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MeContext"}}}}}}}}},"/members":{"get":{"operationId":"getMembers","tags":["Members"],"summary":"List members","parameters":[{"$ref":"#/components/parameters/Search"},{"$ref":"#/components/parameters/PerPage"},{"$ref":"#/components/parameters/Page"}],"responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"200":{"description":"Paginated list of members","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MembersPage"}}}}}},"post":{"operationId":"postMembers","tags":["Members"],"summary":"Create a member","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MemberCreate"}}}},"responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"201":{"description":"Created","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Member"}}}}}},"402":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/PlanLimitReached","description":"The plan's member limit (limit_members) is reached. Upgrade to a higher plan to add more members."},"422":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/ValidationError"}}}},"/members/{id}":{"parameters":[{"$ref":"#/components/parameters/IdPath"}],"get":{"operationId":"getMembersById","tags":["Members"],"summary":"Retrieve a member","responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Member"}}}}}},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"}}},"patch":{"operationId":"patchMembersById","tags":["Members"],"summary":"Update a member","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MemberUpdate"}}}},"responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Member"}}}}}},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"},"422":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/ValidationError"}}},"put":{"operationId":"putMembersById","tags":["Members"],"summary":"Update a member (synonym of PATCH)","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MemberUpdate"}}}},"responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Member"}}}}}},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"},"422":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/ValidationError"}}},"delete":{"operationId":"deleteMembersById","tags":["Members"],"summary":"Remove a member from your MemberArea","description":"Detaches the user from your current MemberArea. The underlying user\naccount is preserved (they may belong to other MemberAreas).\n","responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"204":{"description":"Removed"},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"}}}},"/members/{memberId}/login-link":{"parameters":[{"in":"path","name":"memberId","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"post":{"operationId":"postMembersByMemberIdLoginLink","tags":["Members"],"summary":"Issue a one-time login link for a member","description":"Returns a signed URL that signs the member in on your MemberArea and\ndrops them on `to`. The link is single-use and short-lived: it expires\nafter `expires_in_minutes` (15 by default, 1440 at most) and the\nsignature is burned the moment it is followed, so it cannot be replayed.\n\nFetch it at the moment the member clicks and redirect straight to it.\nNever store it, log it, or put it in a page a third party can read: for\nas long as it is valid it IS the member's session.\n\nRefused with 403 `member_is_admin` for admins and superadmins of the\nbusiness, so an API key can never mint an admin session.\n\nRequired scope: `members:login`.\n","requestBody":{"required":false,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MemberLoginLinkCreate"}}}},"responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"403":{"description":"The API key lacks the members:login scope, or the member is an admin of this business (code member_is_admin).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FrameworkError"}}}},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"201":{"description":"The login link","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MemberLoginLink"}}}}}},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"},"422":{"description":"Validation failed, or this MemberArea has no domain configured (code domain_missing).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FrameworkError"}}}}}}},"/members/{memberId}/tags/{tagId}":{"parameters":[{"in":"path","name":"memberId","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}},{"in":"path","name":"tagId","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"post":{"operationId":"postMembersByMemberIdTagsByTagId","tags":["Members","Tags"],"summary":"Attach a tag to a member","responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"200":{"description":"Attached","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"attached":{"type":"boolean"}}}}}}}},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"}}},"delete":{"operationId":"deleteMembersByMemberIdTagsByTagId","tags":["Members","Tags"],"summary":"Detach a tag from a member","responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"204":{"description":"Detached"},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"}}}},"/members/{memberId}/custom-fields":{"parameters":[{"in":"path","name":"memberId","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"get":{"operationId":"getMembersByMemberIdCustomFields","tags":["Members","Custom Fields"],"summary":"List a member's custom field values","responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MemberCustomFieldValue"}}}}}}}}}},"/members/{memberId}/custom-fields/{fieldId}":{"parameters":[{"in":"path","name":"memberId","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}},{"in":"path","name":"fieldId","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"put":{"operationId":"putMembersByMemberIdCustomFieldsByFieldId","tags":["Members","Custom Fields"],"summary":"Set a member's value for a custom field","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"description":"String, number, boolean or array depending on the field type."}}}}}},"responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"200":{"description":"Saved","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"saved":{"type":"boolean"}}}}}}}}}}},"/members/{memberId}/affiliate":{"parameters":[{"in":"path","name":"memberId","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"get":{"operationId":"getMembersByMemberIdAffiliate","tags":["Members","Affiliates"],"summary":"Retrieve the member's own affiliate account","description":"Returns the affiliate account this member owns: referral code, referral\nURL and the sponsor one level above them. This is the read-only\ncounterpart to `POST /affiliates`, which creates or restores an account\nas a side effect, so ask here whether a member is already a partner.\nInactive affiliates are returned as well, flagged by `is_active`, while\na member without an account and a soft-deleted account both answer 404.\nNot to be confused with the affiliate claim, which records who referred\nthis member. Requires the `affiliates:read` scope.\n","responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"200":{"description":"The affiliate account behind the member","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Affiliate"}}}}}},"403":{"description":"API key lacks the affiliates:read scope.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FrameworkError"}}}},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"}}}},"/members/{memberId}/affiliate-claim":{"parameters":[{"in":"path","name":"memberId","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"get":{"operationId":"getMembersByMemberIdAffiliateClaim","tags":["Members","Affiliates"],"summary":"Retrieve the member's affiliate claim","description":"Returns the affiliate this member is manually assigned to, if any. Claimed members credit every future payment to that affiliate as a commission, even without a referral link. A referral code captured on the purchase itself always takes priority over the claim.\n","responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AffiliateClaim"}}}}}},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"}}},"put":{"operationId":"putMembersByMemberIdAffiliateClaim","tags":["Members","Affiliates"],"summary":"Assign the member to an affiliate","description":"Creates or replaces the member's affiliate claim. Requires the `affiliates:write` scope. Idempotent: repeating the call with the same affiliate code returns 200 with the existing claim.\n","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["affiliate_code"],"properties":{"affiliate_code":{"type":"string","maxLength":64,"description":"Referral code of the affiliate inside this business."}}}}}},"responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"201":{"description":"Claim created","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AffiliateClaim"}}}}}},"200":{"description":"Claim replaced or unchanged","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AffiliateClaim"}}}}}},"403":{"description":"API key lacks the affiliates:write scope.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FrameworkError"}}}},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"},"422":{"description":"Affiliate inactive, or member is the affiliate's own user.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FrameworkError"}}}}}},"delete":{"operationId":"deleteMembersByMemberIdAffiliateClaim","tags":["Members","Affiliates"],"summary":"Remove the member's affiliate claim","responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"204":{"description":"Removed"},"403":{"description":"API key lacks the affiliates:write scope.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FrameworkError"}}}},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"}}}},"/members/{memberId}/reward-balance":{"parameters":[{"in":"path","name":"memberId","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"get":{"operationId":"getMembersByMemberIdRewardBalance","tags":["Members","Affiliates"],"summary":"Read a member's redeemable affiliate reward balance","description":"Returns the member's redeemable affiliate reward per currency: approved-but-unpaid (\"locked\") commission, net of redemptions already booked. Amounts are integers in the smallest currency unit. Use this to credit a member's reward against billing you run yourself (on your own Stripe account). Memberarea never touches your Stripe. Requires the `affiliates:redeem` scope.\n","responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"200":{"description":"OK","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/RewardBalance"}}}}}},"403":{"description":"API key lacks the affiliates:redeem scope.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FrameworkError"}}}},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"}}}},"/members/{memberId}/reward-redemptions":{"parameters":[{"in":"path","name":"memberId","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"post":{"operationId":"postMembersByMemberIdRewardRedemptions","tags":["Members","Affiliates"],"summary":"Redeem part of a member's reward balance","description":"Consumes `amount` from the member's redeemable balance and returns the remaining balance. Call this after you have applied the equivalent discount/credit on your own side. Idempotent: repeating the call with the same `idempotency_key` returns the original result with `idempotent: true` and does not debit twice. A redemption permanently reduces the member's balance and nets against any later cash payout, so the reward cannot be paid twice. Requires the `affiliates:redeem` scope.\n","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["amount","currency","idempotency_key"],"properties":{"amount":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"Minor units (e.g. cents) to redeem."},"currency":{"type":"string","description":"ISO-4217, must match a balance currency."},"idempotency_key":{"type":"string","minLength":8,"maxLength":100}}}}}},"responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthorized"},"429":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/RateLimited"},"201":{"description":"Redeemed","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/RewardRedemption"}}}}}},"200":{"description":"Duplicate (idempotent replay)","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/RewardRedemption"}}}}}},"403":{"description":"API key lacks the affiliates:redeem scope.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FrameworkError"}}}},"404":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/NotFound"},"422":{"description":"Requested amount exceeds the redeemable balance, or no balance in this currency.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FrameworkError"}}}}}}},"/members/by-email":{"get":{"operationId":"getMembersByEmail","tags":["Members"],"summary":"Look up a member by email","description":"Exact email lookup, scoped to the business. Returns a single member.","parameters":[{"in":"query","name":"email","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"email"}}],"responses":{"default":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/UnexpectedError"},"401":{"$ref":"#/components/responses/Unauthori